WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.989
Speaker 1: All sorts of different right wing
media types on the Internet have increasingly

00:00:03.989 --> 00:00:09.830
been talking about a civil war, a civil war
that they believe is coming and in some sense

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:13.470
a civil war that some of them seem to actually
be welcoming.

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:18.380
And whether it is because of those individuals
or for other reasons.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:24.420
We now have two in five Americans, roughly
40% of Americans who believe that within the

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.939
next decade there is going to be another civil
war here in the United States.

00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:35.320
Now, when we say civil war and United States,
what we think back to is the Civil War in

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:40.100
the United States, of course, in the 19th
century, which was a war essentially over

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:45.050
slavery, it was between the Union and the
Confederacy, the union which wanted to end

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:48.170
slavery and the Confederacy which wanted to
keep it.

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:54.990
Now, there's been revisionist history which
has been done to sort of glorify the Confederacy

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:56.990
or at least make it seem more benign.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:01:03.050
And usually the way that's done is they say
it's not about a war to keep slavery.

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:08.119
It's a war for states rights, a fundamental
conservative value.

00:01:08.119 --> 00:01:14.079
And sure, if what the states wanted a right
to do was to keep slavery illegal, then so

00:01:14.079 --> 00:01:15.079
be it.

00:01:15.079 --> 00:01:16.539
But really, it wasn't about slavery.

00:01:16.539 --> 00:01:17.539
It was about states.

00:01:17.539 --> 00:01:18.579
Right now that's B.S.

00:01:18.579 --> 00:01:23.780
doesn't we don't have to get into more detail,
but that is the the false story that many

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:28.259
of those who I guess today would still be
on the side of the Confederacy.

00:01:28.259 --> 00:01:32.130
Like that's the story they like to tell about
the first civil war.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:37.119
And now we have an Economist YouGov poll wherein
40% of Americans believe we are heading towards

00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:38.119
another civil war.

00:01:38.119 --> 00:01:42.479
Now, let's look at a couple of the different
things that are in this poll.

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:48.780
First and foremost, do Americans expect political
divisions and violence to increase over the

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:51.389
next few years?

00:01:51.389 --> 00:01:56.859
And the answer is that on political divisions,
two thirds of Americans believe we will be

00:01:56.859 --> 00:02:02.920
more politically divided, and that political
division is likely to increase.

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:10.640
And on political violence, 65% believe that
political violence has increased.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:14.630
And looking ahead, 62% believe it will continue
to increase.

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:16.950
Now, what is the partizan split here?

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:22.790
This is very, very important for those who
say that in the last year and a half, the

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:26.330
country has become more divided.

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:30.750
Republicans are more likely than independents
and Democrats to say that.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.580
Now, what has happened during that time?

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:35.640
Well, a Democrat, Joe Biden, became president
of the United States.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.360
The mere presence of Biden, they believe,
has made the country more divided.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:44.290
And if you look at looking ahead, do you think
the amount of political division is more likely

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:46.460
to increase, stay the same or decrease?

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:50.019
It is Republicans more than Democrats that
believe political division will increase,

00:02:50.019 --> 00:02:51.470
but it's not a big difference.

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:56.470
This is actually quite interesting because
it's only a 14 point split.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:03:00.780
The country is mostly on the same page, both
Republicans and Democrats.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:06.680
58% of Democrats think there will be more
political division and 72% of Republicans.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:10.799
It is a difference, but it is not a dramatic
partizan difference.

00:03:10.799 --> 00:03:16.390
Now, on the issue of civil war, this is very,
very important and disturbing.

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:19.590
Take a look at these numbers.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:26.879
Among adult citizens in general, 43% say it
is very or somewhat likely that there will

00:03:26.879 --> 00:03:30.329
be another civil war in the next ten years.

00:03:30.329 --> 00:03:35.130
And this is where the partizan split is somewhat
more significant.

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:39.430
Among Democrats, those, for example, who are
strong Democrats.

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:46.170
40% believe a civil war is very or somewhat
likely, whereas among strong Republicans,

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:50.579
54% believe a civil war is very or somewhat
likely.

00:03:50.579 --> 00:03:52.499
That is a significant difference.

00:03:52.499 --> 00:03:55.549
But also, it's not like the 7020 type thing.

00:03:55.549 --> 00:04:02.340
You know, you there are questions you can
ask people and the partizan split is significantly

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:03.340
more dramatic.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:07.510
I'm struggling to think of which ones they
would be, but on issues related to, for example,

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:10.609
guns, sometimes you see a massive partizan
split.

00:04:10.609 --> 00:04:16.590
14 points on civil war is not like a dramatic
split.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:24.050
Now, where I believe you would see a significant
difference would be if you ask folks, what

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:28.130
do you believe would cause such a civil war?

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:30.500
What do you believe would cause such a civil
war?

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:35.310
My instinct is and this is something that
you would have to do a poll on.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:39.990
If you ask the left wingers, what do you think
would cause the Civil War?

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:45.910
I think most left wingers would say right
wingers launching a civil war.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:51.370
And if you asked the right wingers what would
cause a civil war, I think they would mostly

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:55.610
say the left wingers would cause a civil war.

00:04:55.610 --> 00:05:02.849
In other words, I think in different terms
you would see both the left and the right

00:05:02.849 --> 00:05:08.180
say that it would be the right that would
precipitate and take action on that civil

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:09.180
war.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:12.250
The leftists would say the right wingers are
going to do it because they don't like the

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:14.220
ways in which society is changing.

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:17.740
And the right wingers would say, we had no
choice because look what the leftists were

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:19.590
doing to our country.

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:24.600
Very different moral frameworks in terms of
who is responsible.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:30.539
But I think it would be, in a sense, an agreement
in that it would be the rightists who actually

00:05:30.539 --> 00:05:31.699
launch it.

00:05:31.699 --> 00:05:34.699
And the rightist would say, well, we had no
choice because of what the leftists have done

00:05:34.699 --> 00:05:36.330
to this country.

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:38.319
Not particularly pleasing numbers.

00:05:38.319 --> 00:05:43.580
I mean, when nearly half the country thinks
in the next decade there will be a civil war.

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:46.780
It doesn't seem to be boding particularly
well.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:49.539
We're going to follow these numbers and it
would be good to have other polling as well,

00:05:49.539 --> 00:05:52.200
because it is increasingly a topic.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:56.349
I mean, later in the show, actually, we're
going to have a clip of conspiracy theorist

00:05:56.349 --> 00:06:01.729
Alex Jones who just got dinged for 49 million
in a defamation suit.

00:06:01.729 --> 00:06:05.639
He seems to be trying to precipitate that
civil war and is predicting it.

00:06:05.639 --> 00:06:10.460
I think within the I think he said in 71 days,
oddly specific.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:54.169
But we'll get to that Alex Jones clip a little
bit later on 

00:06:54.169 --> 00:07:14.069
in 

00:07:14.069 --> 00:07:14.990
the show.

